#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: sunless sea.
#> pause: 45
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan + A stately pleasure dome decree:
#> must: Where Alph, the sacred river, ran + Through caverns measureless to man
#> must: Down to a sunless sea.
#> not: man + Down
#> not: decree: + Where
#> source: $!N
# 15. N: two input lines in one pattern space. McMahon 1.3, 3.4
# Ordinarily the pattern space holds one line. N appends the next input line
# to it, with a newline in between, so a pattern can match across lines and
# an s can edit the newline itself: \n is that imbedded newline. $!N means
# "unless this is the last line" (! is explained in step 18); line 5 has no
# partner, and is written alone. Lines are consumed in pairs: 1+2, 3+4, 5.
# Try: replace " + " with "\n" to put the two lines back.
$!N
s/\n/ + /

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
